    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i>Sorter</i>, you\u2019re dropped into a mysterious facility with one simple directive: organize the chaos. Sort vibrant cubes into the correct chutes. Build stairways, bridges, and towers to navigate an ever-evolving environment. Master the laws of falling-object physics. Then do it all again\u2014only better, faster, and smarter.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But under the surface of this serene sorting simulator lies something... strange. Clues hide in plain sight. Patterns whisper. As you unlock new abilities and advance through each handcrafted level, a deeper question begins to take shape:<br><strong>Why are you here?</strong></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83e\udde0 <strong>Chill first-person puzzle gameplay</strong> focused on logic, color (or shapes), and spatial thinking.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83e\uddf1 <strong>Build with purpose</strong>\u2014use cubes to create paths, solve challenges, or just make something oddly satisfying.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udf00 <strong>Unlock new abilities\u00a0</strong>that reshape how you interact with the world\u2014and the cubes in it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udd75\ufe0f <strong>Uncover a hidden narrative</strong>\u2014told not with words, but with puzzles, visuals, and implication.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83e\uddd8 <strong>Meditative vibes</strong> with no timers, no enemies, just you and a lot of cubes with secrets.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Sorter</i> is more than just a puzzle game. It\u2019s an invitation to sort through not just objects\u2026 but ideas.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i>Sorter</i>, you\u2019re dropped into a mysterious facility with one simple directive: organize the chaos. Sort vibrant cubes into the correct chutes. Build stairways, bridges, and towers to navigate an ever-evolving environment. Master the laws of falling-object physics. Then do it all again\u2014only better, faster, and smarter.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But under the surface of this serene sorting simulator lies something... strange. Clues hide in plain sight. Patterns whisper. As you unlock new abilities and advance through each handcrafted level, a deeper question begins to take shape:<br><strong>Why are you here?</strong></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83e\udde0 <strong>Chill first-person puzzle gameplay</strong> focused on logic, color (or shapes), and spatial thinking.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83e\uddf1 <strong>Build with purpose</strong>\u2014use cubes to create paths, solve challenges, or just make something oddly satisfying.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udf00 <strong>Unlock new abilities\u00a0</strong>that reshape how you interact with the world\u2014and the cubes in it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udd75\ufe0f <strong>Uncover a hidden narrative</strong>\u2014told not with words, but with puzzles, visuals, and implication.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83e\uddd8 <strong>Meditative vibes</strong> with no timers, no enemies, just you and a lot of cubes with secrets.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Sorter</i> is more than just a puzzle game. It\u2019s an invitation to sort through not just objects\u2026 but ideas.</p>",
